# Build artifacts
build/
out/
*.dll
*.pdb
*.log

# Release packaging (build-release.ps1) -- release-staging/ is staged from THIS repo's own tree
# by sync-release-staging.ps1 and is gitignored because it is a build input, not source.
# github-releases/ is the built zip output, a reproducible artifact.
release-staging/
github-releases/

# --- Python runtime (the proxy now lives in this repo) ---
# CREDENTIAL GUARDS. This repo is public and the proxy writes live secrets into this folder at
# runtime, so none of these may ever be committable:
#   config.json            - API keys (values saved via the dashboard are `enc:`-encrypted; keys
#                            written directly can still be plaintext). RELEASING.md calls this the
#                            single highest-risk file in the project.
#   .proxy.key             - the Fernet key proxy_internal/encryption.py generates to decrypt the
#                            `enc:` values above. Committing it alongside an encrypted config is
#                            equivalent to committing the plaintext keys.
#   antigravity-auth.json  - live Antigravity OAuth tokens (proxy.py ANTIGRAVITY_AUTH_FILE).
#   proxy.ini / *.log      - personal paths, per-user settings, real request history.
# These lines are what keeps `git add -A` from publishing credentials.
config.json
.proxy.key
antigravity-auth.json
proxy.ini
stats.json
*.log
# Atomic-write leftovers: auth/antigravity.py writes .<name>.XXXX.tmp in this
# directory before renaming, so a crash mid-write would otherwise leave a file
# holding token material sitting in the repo root.
*.tmp

